# {{flow_name}} flow rubric

## Critical — FAIL if any fail
1. `/mnt/session/outputs/manifest.json` exists and is valid JSON
2. `manifest.site_dir` equals `"."` and `manifest.ready_to_deploy` is `true`
3. `/mnt/session/outputs/index.html` exists and is non-empty (Files API flattens subdirectories — write FLAT at the outputs root)
4. `index.html` contains a `<title>` tag with text "{{site_title}}"
5. `index.html` parses as valid HTML5 (no unclosed tags in the first error from a strict parser)

## Quality — flag but do not fail
6. Page renders without errors at 1280×800 desktop viewport
7. Page is mobile-responsive at 375×667
8. No external requests fail (broken CDN links, missing fonts)

## Post-hook — graded outside the session
The host post_session_hook deploys the site to Vercel AFTER the agent
session ends and appends `manifest.page_url` + `manifest.deployed_at`.
That work is not gradable by the in-session rubric (the agent cannot
make `page_url` true). Check the saved outputs dir for the final
manifest.
